### NEW: python/plan_provenance.py
- Add a small shared parser for the Step 5c provenance header:
- Read only leading lines before the first blank line (or EOF when no blank line).
- Parse `review_status: <token>` when present; validate against an allowlist (`complete`, `cap-hit`, `panel-failed`, `panel-init-failed`, `panel-skipped`, and other statuses Step 5c may write).
- Parse `rounds_completed: <N>` when present; require a non-negative integer.
- Return structured fields plus `header_present` booleans so callers can distinguish missing provenance from explicit refusal values.
- Ignore any `review_status:` / `rounds_completed:` matches in the plan body below the header.
- Expose `plan-provenance parse` (or `plan-block parse-provenance`) via `cli.py` for shell callers.
